{"title":"eBike Popemobile for Leo XIV, from Scott","link":"https://bikerumor.com/ebike-popemobile-for-leo-xiv-from-scott/","date":1795646269000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_subtle-headtube-detail-1536x1024.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Scott SUB Tour 10 Wave city commuter Popemobile for Pope Leo XIV: papal headbadge\" /></p>\n<p>We’ve watched cycling brands build custom bikes for Popes for more than a decade, yet Scott’s new papal edition of their Sub Tour 10 Wave city ebike looks like something Pope Leo XIV might actually want to ride. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Scott teamed up with the UCI to create this special papal edition urban ebike and a matching helmet to commemorate Pope Leo XIV’s “<em>shared values of mobility, accessibility, and connection</em>“. At the Vatican this week, Scott and the UCI presented the functional ebike to the Pope, citing bicycles’ role both as recreation, but also as a source of freedom to those who ride. </p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote>\n<p>“Cycling can therefore be understood as a metaphor for that ‘life in abundance’ that is characteristic of every authentic sporting experience.”</p>\n<cite><em>– Pope Leo XIV</em></cite></blockquote>\n\n\n\n<h2>Scott’s ebike Popemobile: Sub Tour 10 Wave city commuter</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican.jpg\"><img width=\"2400\" height=\"1800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican.jpg\" alt=\"Scott SUB Tour 10 Wave city commuter Popemobile for Pope Leo XIV\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_no-nonsense-papal-city-bike-for-getting-around-the-Vatican-1200x900.jpg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption><i>(All photos/Scott Sports)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Sure, a custom <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/purchase-the-popes-pinarello-papal-dogma-gifted-by-giro-winner-egan-bernal-on-auction/\" target=\"_blank\">papal Pinarello</a> for the previous Pope Francis was slick, as was getting a custom <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/closeup-pope-francis-custom-specialized-venge-road-bike-is-one-helluva-holy-roller/\" target=\"_blank\">S-Works Venge</a> and a rainbow jersey <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/pope-rides-specialized-thanks-peter-sagan/\" target=\"_blank\">from World Champ Peter Sagan</a>. But maybe more realistic were the classic <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/forget-the-pope-mobile-papa-francisco-now-has-a-custom-breezer-downtown-8/\" target=\"_blank\">Breezer Downtown</a> townie or the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/can-riding-a-bike-make-you-more-holy-daimler-gives-pope-francis-a-smart-ebike/\" target=\"_blank\">Smart eBike</a> from Daimler that he received earliest in his tenure, while already 76-years-old with just one lung.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>But let’s be honest, Popes are rarely spring chickens. The Chicago-borne Pope Leo XIV is already 71-years-old, and just had part of his lung quickly removed after a recent lung cancer diagnosis. So, a step-through city ebike sounds like a much more appropriate gift for the holy septuagenarian.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Custom Papal edition graphics</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet.jpg\" alt=\"Scott SUB Tour 10 Wave city commuter Popemobile for Pope Leo XIV: papal helmet\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_matching-low-key-helmet-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Scott custom painted both the Sub Tour 10 Wave city ebike and a matching Sierra MIPS helmet to keep the papal head safe and sound zipping around town.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Seriously, this is maybe the most subdued papal paint job &amp; graphics we’ve seen customize on a bike for the head of the Catholic Church. But that actually seems more fitting for the Pope, right? </p>\n\n\n\n<p>What you get is just a silver monochromatic coat of arms Pope Leo XIV on a frame with a subtle white marble finish. Scott says the look was inspired by the 4-wheeled Popemobile – which currently is a pearl-white electric Mercedes G580, <em><s>heavenly</s> heavily</em> customized itself, of course. So yes, now Pope Leo XIV has two custom electric rides to cruise around Vatican City.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Tech details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail.jpg\"><img width=\"1333\" height=\"2000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail.jpg\" alt=\"Scott SUB Tour 10 Wave city commuter Popemobile for Pope Leo XIV: papal front end detail\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail.jpg 1333w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail-200x300.jpg 200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail-80x120.jpg 80w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_detail-600x900.jpg 600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>step-through alloy frame ebike</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bosch Performance Line CX motor: max 100Nm torque &amp; 750W peak power</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bosch PowerTube 800Wh internal battery – removable</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Shimano Nexus Inter 5e, 5-speed internal gear hub</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Gates CDX belt drive</li>\n\n\n\n<li>100mm SR Suntour XCM34 BOOST AIR LO suspension fork</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Shimano MT200 2-piston hydraulic brakes with 180/160mm rotors</li>\n\n\n\n<li>adjustable height stem with integrated SP Connect phone mount</li>\n\n\n\n<li>integrated Lezyne front and rear lights</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ursus U-mount kickstand</li>\n\n\n\n<li>sadly, no dropper for the Pope though</li>\n\n\n\n<li>700x55mm Schwalbe Big Apple Performance tires</li>\n\n\n\n<li>full-coverage fenders</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Racktime rack with SnapIt 2.0 &amp; Kid’nCarry mounting: max 30kg load rated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>29.7kg/65.5lb claimed complete weight</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3>Scott ebike Popemobile – Pricing &amp; availability</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit.jpg\"><img width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit.jpg\" alt=\"Scott SUB Tour 10 Wave city commuter Popemobile for Pope Leo XIV: custom papal kit\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Scott-SUB-Tour-10-Wave-city-commuter-Popemobile-for-Pope-Leo-XIV_papal-custom-kit-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>A papal Scott ebike is pretty much free and readily available. All you need to do is make it out of the next conclave.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Otherwise, you could get a <a href=\"https://www.scott-sports.com/global/en/product/scott-sub-tour-10-wave-bike\" target=\"_blank\">regular-edition</a> Sub Tour 10 ebike of your own for 4400€ with the same spec as Pope Leo XIV. Its standard colors are even named fit for the devout: Celestial silver or Paradise green. Perfect for getting around your own <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_City\" target=\"_blank\">sovereign city-state</a>, or just the regular town where you live. We don’t know what size the Pope rides, but it comes in four options (S-XL).</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.scott-sports.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Scott-sports.com</a></em></p>","author":"Cory Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/ebike-popemobile-for-leo-xiv-from-scott/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"9db25580afc038e6ce4470013d0c39c4fea52ea102c4f93ead10dafb655f7be7","category":"Cycling"}